<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Stalingrad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1942">1942</a>–<a href="/years/1943">1943</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volgograd">Stalingrad</a> was fought from August 1942 to February 1943 for the city of Stalingrad, now Volgograd, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a>. After German forces took most of the city in brutal street fighting, the Soviet Operation Uranus in November 1942 encircled the Sixth Army, whose remnants surrendered under Friedrich Paulus on 2 February 1943. With casualties of around two million in all, it marked a turning point of the war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-stalingrad.jpg" alt="Battle of Stalingrad" width="330" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Расчет_советской_76,2-мм_пушки_ЗиС-3_ведет_огонь_в_Сталинграде._Ноябрь_1942_г.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Defeat at the <b>Battle of Stalingrad</b>, where the Sixth Army surrendered in early 1943, and the failed offensive at the Battle of Kursk that July lost the initiative in the east.</blockquote><a href="/empire/nazi-germany">Nazi Germany · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…the Second World War it bore much of the fighting after Germany invaded on 22 June 1941: Leningrad endured a siege of almost 900 days, the Germans were stopped before Moscow in December 1941, and the battles of <b>Stalingrad</b> in 1942–1943 and Kursk in 1943 turned the war.</blockquote><a href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Russian SFSR · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…catastrophic losses, but the Red Army halted the Germans at Moscow in December 1941, destroyed an entire German army at <b>Stalingrad</b> in 1942–1943, won the tank battle at Kursk in July 1943 and smashed Army Group Centre in Operation Bagration in 1944, before taking Berlin in May 1945.</blockquote><a href="/empire/soviet-union">Soviet Union · Military</a></li></ul></section>
